# inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded Design

Date: 2026-06-27

Status: Implemented first pass in the UnrealMCP editor bridge after explicit
Ieta/Tivret proceed request. Keep future changes read-only and non-simulating.

Scope: editor-only, read-only PhysicsAsset inventory for animation physics
work. Runtime/gameplay code, simulation, and asset mutation are out of scope.

## Purpose

`inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded` is a narrow UnrealMCP
bridge command for requests that need PhysicsAsset body, constraint, profile,
and solver information without mutating or simulating anything.

The command should help animation work around RigidBody AnimGraph nodes,
secondary motion, ragdoll setup review, and physical animation profiles by
returning bounded, structured data from `UPhysicsAsset`.

The command exists because current MCP tools can set a narrow subset of
RigidBody AnimGraph node settings, but they do not expose the PhysicsAsset
bodies, constraints, limits, drives, or profiles that explain the node's asset
inputs.

## Ieta Review

Request class: inspect PhysicsAsset bodies, collision shape counts,
constraints, limits, drives, constraint profiles, physical animation profiles,
or RBAN solver settings for animation work.

Existing routes checked:

- `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings` can read RigidBody AnimGraph node settings.
- `set_anim_graph_rigidbody_settings` can modify a narrow sample RigidBody
  AnimGraph node.
- `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose` can prove selected node behavior for
  supported cases.

Why existing routes are insufficient: they do not read the PhysicsAsset's
`SkeletalBodySetups`, `ConstraintSetup`, body geometry summaries, profile data,
or RBAN solver settings.

Asset mutation boundary: read-only. The command must not save, compile, tick,
simulate, cook collision, apply profiles to components, or mark packages dirty.

Implemented command: `inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded`.

Default safety guard: load only a `UPhysicsAsset` or resolve one from a supplied
`USkeletalMesh`; bound arrays by caller-provided limits; return
`unsupported_class` for other assets.

Approval state: user approved Ieta/Tivret to proceed. This command is limited to
the UnrealMCP editor bridge and does not add runtime/gameplay code.

## UE 5.6 API Anchors

Use installed UE 5.6 headers as local truth:

| Need | UE 5.6 anchor | Safe access rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PhysicsAsset body and constraint arrays | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/PhysicsEngine/PhysicsAsset.h` | Read `SkeletalBodySetups`, `ConstraintSetup`, `SolverSettings`, profile names, and preview mesh only. |
| Body setup and physical animation profiles | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/PhysicsEngine/SkeletalBodySetup.h` | Read `GetPhysicalAnimationProfiles()` and `bSkipScaleFromAnimation`; do not add, remove, rename, or update profiles. |
| Collision geometry summary | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/PhysicsEngine/BodySetup.h` and `AggregateGeom.h` | Report counts and simple extents from `AggGeom`; avoid unbounded convex vertex dumps. |
| Constraint template | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/PhysicsEngine/PhysicsConstraintTemplate.h` | Read `DefaultInstance` and `ProfileHandles`; do not call editor mutation helpers. |
| Constraint instance | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/PhysicsEngine/ConstraintInstance.h` | Use getters for bone names, linear limits, angular limits, projection, breakability, plasticity, and drives. |
| SkeletalMesh fallback | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Engine/SkeletalMesh.h` | If a mesh path is supplied, resolve its PhysicsAsset only as read-only input. |

## Command Schema

Proposed input fields:

| Field | Type | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `physics_asset_path` | string | optional | Preferred explicit `UPhysicsAsset` path. |
| `skeletal_mesh_path` | string | optional | Resolve PhysicsAsset from mesh when asset path is absent. |
| `include_bodies` | bool | `true` | Include body setup summaries. |
| `include_constraints` | bool | `true` | Include constraint summaries. |
| `include_profiles` | bool | `true` | Include constraint and physical animation profile names and bounded settings. |
| `include_solver_settings` | bool | `true` | Include RBAN solver settings. |
| `include_collision_summary` | bool | `true` | Include shape counts and bounded simple dimensions. |
| `max_bodies` | int | `128` | Truncate body list above this count. |
| `max_constraints` | int | `128` | Truncate constraint list above this count. |
| `max_profiles_per_item` | int | `16` | Truncate per-body or per-constraint profiles. |
| `max_shapes_per_body` | int | `32` | Truncate detailed shape summaries per body. |

At least one of `physics_asset_path` or `skeletal_mesh_path` is required.

## Response Schema

Return structured evidence:

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `success` | Whether inspection completed. |
| `physics_asset_path` | Resolved PhysicsAsset path. |
| `source_skeletal_mesh_path` | Mesh path when used for resolution. |
| `preview_skeletal_mesh` | PhysicsAsset preview mesh when available. |
| `solver_settings` | RBAN solver settings summary. |
| `constraint_profile_names` | Asset-level constraint profile names. |
| `physical_animation_profile_names` | Asset-level or per-body physical animation profile names. |
| `body_count` | Total bodies before truncation. |
| `constraint_count` | Total constraints before truncation. |
| `bodies` | Bounded body summaries. |
| `constraints` | Bounded constraint summaries. |
| `truncated` | Per-section truncation flags and omitted counts. |
| `warnings` | Missing meshes, null entries, unsupported fields, or skipped detail. |

Body summaries should include body name, body index, bounds-body flag,
collision trace/collision enabled summary when safely available, geometry
counts, simple shape dimensions, mass override summary when available, and
physical animation profile summaries.

Constraint summaries should include constraint index, joint name, child and
parent bone names, profile names, linear limit/motion, angular swing and twist
limits/motions, projection flags, breakability, plasticity, disable-collision,
parent-dominates, mass-conditioning, and drive enable/target summaries.

## Guardrails

Forbidden patterns:

- starting, ticking, or sampling physics simulation;
- applying constraint profiles to component instances;
- calling editor mutation helpers such as add, remove, rename, duplicate, or
  update profile functions;
- saving, compiling, cooking collision, or rebuilding body setups;
- dumping unbounded convex hull vertices, cooked data, or private binary
  collision buffers;
- broad Python reflection over every property of `UPhysicsAsset`,
  `USkeletalBodySetup`, or `FConstraintInstance`;
- using the inspector as proof of runtime RigidBody node output.

Keep claims limited to static source PhysicsAsset data unless paired with a
separate runtime probe.

## Verification

Docs-only verification for this design:

- `git diff --check`
- Markdown link and trailing-whitespace sanity checks.

Implementation verification:

1. Inspect a PhysicsAsset by direct path and confirm body/constraint counts
   match the asset arrays.
2. Inspect the same asset via a SkeletalMesh path and confirm the resolved path
   matches.
3. Confirm null body or constraint entries are reported as warnings rather than
   crashes.
4. Confirm truncation flags are set when limits are exceeded.
5. Confirm no package is dirty after inspection.
6. Pair with `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings` only when the user also needs
   the RigidBody node's AnimGraph settings.

## Tivret Maintenance Notes

When this design becomes an approved implementation task, Tivret should:

- implement a read-only C++ inspector first;
- keep the response bounded and explicit rather than returning raw property
  bags;
- add Python wrapper and server registration only after the C++ response schema
  is stable;
- document the command in `Docs/Tools/node_tools.md` or a narrow animation
  tools document;
- avoid runtime simulation, component mutation, asset saves, collision cooking,
  or gameplay module changes;
- verify with direct asset path, mesh-derived asset path, truncation, and
  no-dirty-package checks.
